{"id":"n2-076","title":"～つつある","romaji":"〜tsutsu aru","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Expresses an ongoing process or gradual change.","longExplanation":"The ～つつある grammar point is used to describe something that is in the middle of a gradual change or development. It can be translated as '(something) is in the process of ~ing.' The most common usage is with the verb stem plus つつある.","formation":"Verb-stem + つつある","examples":[{"jp":"地球温暖化は進行しつつある。","romaji":"Chikyū ondanka wa shinkō shitsutsu aru.","en":"Global warming is in progress.","words":[{"surface":"地球温暖化","vocabId":"1420980","reading":"ちきゅうおんだんか"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"進行","vocabId":"1366060","reading":"しんこう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"つつ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ある","vocabId":"1296400","reading":"ある"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5]},{"jp":"この町は急速に発展しつつある。","romaji":"Kono machi wa kyūsoku ni hatten shitsutsu aru.","en":"This town is rapidly developing.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"町","vocabId":"1603990","reading":"まち"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"急速","vocabId":"1228890","reading":"きゅうそく"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"発展","vocabId":"1477720","reading":"はってん"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"つつ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ある","vocabId":"1296400","reading":"ある"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[7,8]},{"jp":"子供たちは成長しつつある。","romaji":"Kodomo-tachi wa seichō shitsutsu aru.","en":"The children are growing up.","words":[{"surface":"子供たち","vocabId":"1307870","reading":"こどもたち"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"成長","vocabId":"1375790","reading":"せいちょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"つつ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ある","vocabId":"1296400","reading":"ある"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5]},{"jp":"景気が回復しつつある。","romaj